  "about": "How the game places the Country's farms' people and the communities' markets (Docs/Design/71-the-country-s-industries.md, Phase C; the user, 2026-11-03), with Data/Economy/communities.json (the places). When a farm's area is switched on, each of its posts is filled from the unplaced NPCs (doc 66, 2) by old trade, deterministically: its keeper the oldest suitable adult of its trades with family among the unplaced where there is one (the family: spouse, children and parents, up to the farmhouse's beds, living at the farmhouse; one of working age and of the farm's trades works as one of its hands), then its hands (16 to retirement; the farm's own trades first, the fallback trades for what they can't fill), housed in the farm's community (at most `householdMost` a home) or, for a farm near the city, as doc 68's arrivals are. A community's market is staffed when its first farm is: its keepers of the towns' trades and shops, its hands of service and labour. No NPC is made. Each label must hold no business word (communities.json `workLabels`) but a market keeper's, and be at most 40 characters: `{place}` is the steading's name less its `suffixes` (or the farm's own in `places`: Alderbank holds \"bank\", the moneychanger's word), `{name}` the business's. Doc 72's works (communities.json `works` with a `works` id: the woods' and the peat's; Phase 3's granite quarry and clay pits, of the mines, stone and clay, a pit one hand and no keeper) are placed the same way, with no farmhouse: their keepers, of those with no family among the unplaced first, come alone and live with the hands (in the works' community, or in the city as arrivals do), and their posts are out of doors at the works.",
